{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "U1 & U2: Implement and expose SDK inter-process communication / REST gateway wrappers and sample applications allowing Node.js applications to interact with Java and Python SDK runtimes and Hyperledger Fabric networks.",
    "U3: Extend peer chaincode package/install routines to support pre-compiled binaries and Docker containers as User Chaincode (UCC) packages, bypassing source compilation on peer nodes.",
    "U4: Enhance the Validation System Chaincode (VSCC) policy evaluation module to inspect identity MSPs and policy trees upon evaluation failure, outputting human-readable signer/organization validation breakdowns at INFO/DEBUG log levels and including detail payloads in tx failure events.",
    "U5: Extend the release Makefile and CI pipelines to cross-compile platform-specific release binaries (Linux, macOS, Windows) for configtxgen, fabric-chaintool, fabric-ca-client, and related binaries.",
    "U6: Implement certificate fingerprint verification within Fabric MSP/Auth Handlers, supporting channel configuration settings for pinned root/intermediate CA fingerprints.",
    "U7: Update Sphinx/ReadTheDocs documentation (`testing.html`) with guides and cross-links to test harnesses under `fabric/test/` for fast local network bootstrap and custom chaincode testing.",
    "U8: Create a standardized `sampleconfig/config_defaults` directory containing fully populated `core.yaml`, `orderer.yaml`, and `configtx.yaml` files documenting all default values extracted from Go source initializers."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "All development, testing, and documentation will be completed by a single experienced Go and Hyperledger Fabric developer.",
    "Target platforms for platform-specific binaries include Linux (x86_64, s390x, arm64), macOS (x86_64), and Windows (x86_64).",
    "Existing fabric test networks (e.g., BYFN / Bootstrap scripts) are available as references for quickstart docs.",
    "VSCC enhancements do not break determinism across endorsing and committing peers."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-1",
      "activity_name": "U1 & U2: Node.js Integration & Polyglot SDK Interoperability Samples",
      "activity_description": "Develop integration wrappers, documentation, and sample applications demonstrating Node.js application interaction with Java and Python Fabric SDK environments.",
      "most_likely_effort": 60
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-2",
      "activity_name": "U3: Pre-built User Chaincode (UCC) Deployment Mechanism",
      "activity_description": "Modify chaincode packaging, installation, and launcher logic in the peer to support pre-built chaincode images and binaries without local peer source code compilation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 70
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-3",
      "activity_name": "U4: VSCC Validation Failure Logging & Event Notification Payload Enhancements",
      "activity_description": "Refactor VSCC policy evaluator to produce granular logs detailing evaluated policies, satisfied signers, missing org signatures, and propagate error details to tx validation event notifications.",
      "most_likely_effort": 50
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-4",
      "activity_name": "U5: Platform Binary Build Automation & Packaging Scripts",
      "activity_description": "Update build scripts and Makefile targets to cross-compile and tar/zip release binaries (configtxgen, fabric-chaintool, fabric-ca-client) across Linux, macOS, and Windows platforms.",
      "most_likely_effort": 40
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-5",
      "activity_name": "U6: Certificate Fingerprint Pinning & Independent CA Verification",
      "activity_description": "Implement certificate fingerprint validation in the channel MSP configuration and endorsement/auth handler pipelines, including verification against channel-configured fingerprint rules.",
      "most_likely_effort": 90
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-6",
      "activity_name": "U7: Fabric Testing Guide & Quickstart Network Documentation",
      "activity_description": "Author testing documentation in ReadTheDocs (`testing.html`) providing clear quickstart steps to spin up local test networks and linking to scripts in `fabric/test/`.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-7",
      "activity_name": "U8: Consolidated Default Configuration Files (`config_defaults`)",
      "activity_description": "Audit Go source files for internal defaults, create complete `core.yaml`, `orderer.yaml`, and `configtx.yaml` files under `config_defaults/`, and update documentation links.",
      "most_likely_effort": 30
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "ACT-8",
      "activity_name": "System Integration, E2E Verification & Test Suite Execution",
      "activity_description": "Perform end-to-end integration testing, regression test suite execution, and verify cross-platform binary builds and documentation generation.",
      "most_likely_effort": 50
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 414
  }
}
```

